Description: Matrix chat client with end-to-end encryption [Trinity]
 TMatrix is a chat client for Matrix, the open and decentralised network
 for secure communication, made for the Trinity Desktop Environment. It
 works with any homeserver and with people who use other Matrix apps.
 .
 It supports direct chats and rooms, invitations, the public room
 directory, Markdown, replies, edits, reactions, pictures and files, room
 settings and members, several accounts, and a system tray icon with
 unread counts and notifications.
 .
 Direct chats and private rooms are end-to-end encrypted. Sessions are
 verified by comparing emoji and message keys are backed up with a
 recovery key. The protocol and the encryption are implemented by
 matrix-rust-sdk and vodozemac, which are built into the program.
 .
 Building the package needs Rust 1.96 or later (rustup) and network access
 to crates.io.
